  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}$. Let $\\mathrm{R}$ be a relation on $\\mathrm{A}$ defined by $x \\mathrm{R} y$ if and only if $4 x \\leq 5 \\mathrm{y}$. Let $\\mathrm{m}$ be the number of elements in $\\mathrm{R}$ and $\\mathrm{n}$ be the minimum number of elements from $\\mathrm{A} \\times \\mathrm{A}$ that are required to be added to $\\mathrm{R}$ to make it a symmetric relation. Then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "25",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "24",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "26",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "23",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given : $4 x \\leq 5 y$\nthen\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{R}=\\{ & (1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(1,4),(1,5),(2,2),(2,3),(2,4) \\\\\n& (2,5),(3,3),(3,4),(3,5),(4,4),(4,5),(5,4),(5,5)\\}\n\\end{aligned}$\ni.e. 16 elements.\ni.e. $\\mathrm{m}=16$\nNow to make R a symmetric relation add\n$\\{(2,1)(3,2)(4,3)(3,1)(4,2)(5,3)(4,1)(5,2)(5,1)\\}$\ni.e. $n=9$<br />So $m+n=25$"
  }
}